+<!-- evidence-type: analysis -->
+# Standing rule payload, per host
+
+Pinned to commit `9ae0ff2889ce3c30d5cbd9432d659fc624685b2b`. Generated by
+`./scripts-run src/scripts/report_standing_payload_by_host --emit --pin 9ae0ff2889ce3c30d5cbd9432d659fc624685b2b`;
+a re-run at the same pin is byte-identical — no value is read from `$HOME` and no
+timestamp is written.
+
+## The unit, and why it is not this disk
+
+The census is taken over the **projection source** `dist/agent-src/rules`, minus the
+ADR-004 `type: manual` rules no per-tool tree ever receives. That is the UPPER BOUND a
+host loads: an unscoped, un-deduplicated consumer install.
+
+Reading it off the local trees instead would measure this machine. Two install-local
+filters shrink a maintainer checkout below what a consumer receives — user-scope dedup
+(a rule byte-identical to a user-scope twin is skipped) and workspace/pack scope. Both
+are real, both differ per install, and step 0.1 requires a re-run at the same pin to be
+byte-identical. Every scope narrowing moves a host DOWN from the figure below, never up.
+
+**This measures delivery, not consumption.** Whether a host READS what it is handed is
+the axis `docs/enforcement-by-host.md:18-28` owns; a host with a tree it never loads
+would look identical here.
+
+## The rule corpus
+
+| Quantity | Value |
+|---|---:|
+| `.md` files in `dist/agent-src/rules` | 119 |
+| of those, `type: manual` (never projected, ADR-004) | 5 |
+| projected to a per-rule host tree | 114 |
+| bytes of the projected set | 484968 |
+| chars/4 tokens of the projected set | 121242 |
+
+## Per host
+
+| Host | Surface | Shape | Bytes | chars/4 tok | Writer |
+|---|---|---|---:|---:|---|
+| `augment` | `.augment/rules` | per-rule tree | 484968 | 121242 | `src/scripts/condense.ts:2499` |
+| `claude-code` | `.claude/rules` | per-rule tree | 484968 | 121242 | `src/scripts/condense.ts:1192` |
+| `cline` | `.clinerules` | per-rule tree | 484968 | 121242 | `src/scripts/condense.ts:1194` |
+| `copilot` | `.github/copilot-instructions.md` | single file | 7491 | 1873 | `src/scripts/generate_capability_matrix.ts:138` |
+| `cowork` | — | none | — | — | — |
+| `cursor` | `.cursor/rules` | per-rule tree | 484968 | 121242 | `src/scripts/condense.ts:1194` |
+| `gemini` | `GEMINI.md` | single file | 2982 | 746 | `src/scripts/condense.ts:1498` |
+| `windsurf` | `.windsurfrules` | single file | 34180 | 8545 | `src/scripts/condense.ts:1242` |
+| `codex` | `.codex/agent-config.md` | single file | absent | absent | `src/scripts/install.ts:1541` |
+
+Notes per host:
+
+- `augment` — copies by default; symlinks under `augment.rules_use_symlinks`
+- `claude-code` — `_emit_claude_rule` rewrites frontmatter to the host's own `paths:` key
+- `cline` — symlink per rule into the projection
+- `copilot` — NOT written by `condense`: the installer aggregates it from `src/agent-src/templates/copilot-instructions.md`, which is why the capability matrix marks this cell `adapter` and footnotes it as install-time
+- `cowork` — no rule-tree writer in this tree; carries hook bindings only
+- `cursor` — symlink per rule, plus `.mdc` companions at `condense.ts:1422`
+- `gemini` — single file
+- `windsurf` — single concatenated file
+- `codex` — written by the installer, not by `condense`; absent in this checkout
+
+## The two units, recorded once
+
+- **chars/4** is what `check_preamble_payload_budget` reports, and its measured total at
+  this pin is **138,200 tok** across three buckets (project-scope rules 122,608 ·
+  preloaded skills catalog 14,846 · CLAUDE.md hierarchy 746).
+- **Exact BPE** is the unit `docs/CLAIMS.md:365` uses for the delivery experiment:
+  120,582 → 18,573 exact-BPE standing tokens for the rule corpus under
+  `lean_projection.mode: delivery`. The two units are NOT interchangeable and no delta
+  is computed between them here.
+
+**Reconciling the two rule figures, because they differ and both are right.** The
+census bucket reads 122,608 chars/4 tok over the projection directory; the projected-set
+row above reads 121242. The gap is the 5 `type: manual` rules: the census counts every
+`.md` in the directory, this table counts only what a per-tool tree receives. 5465 bytes
+= 1366 tok, and 121242 + 1366 = 122608. A manual rule reaches no host tree
+by ADR-004, so excluding it is correct here and including it is correct there.
+
+## Per-slot delivery fire sizes — the activation charge (3.1)
+
+Gate-open per-fire emission of the `rule-inject` concern over the frozen
+`tests/eval/routing-matrix` corpus, measured through the SAME selection the runtime
+concern uses (`_lib/rule_injection.ts::matchTierRules` + `selectForInjection` at the
+concern's own `CAP_BYTES`), never through a second model of it.
+
+| Slot | Fires | p50 B | p90 B | max B |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| `user_prompt_submit` | 318 | 6674 | 16188 | 20406 |
+| `pre_tool_use` | 32 | 6662 | 19649 | 19649 |
+| `pre_compact` | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
+
+`pre_compact` is zero **by construction, not by measurement**: that branch of
+`rule_inject_hook` clears the seen-set and returns allow without writing to stdout, so
+there is no emission to sample.
+
+**Rules reachable ONLY on `pre_tool_use`**, which is the condition owner ruling E2
+makes the `pre_tool_use` binding conditional on — 3 of them, all labelled:
+
+- `design-review-after-ui-write`
+- `source-of-truth`
+- `ui-audit-gate`
+
+## What the flip must move, and what it must not
+
+`claude-code` is the only host in the default `lean_projection.hosts`. Its row above is
+the number the flip reduces. **Every other per-rule-tree row must stay byte-identical**
+— that is the D1 repair and the Phase 1.4 gate, and it is why this table exists per host
+rather than as one total.
